{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/wieslawsoltes/SharpForge/pulls/4525","id":4733972516,"node_id":"PR_kwDOU59Ms88AAAABGiqwJA","html_url":"https://github.com/wieslawsoltes/SharpForge/pull/4525","diff_url":"https://github.com/wieslawsoltes/SharpForge/pull/4525.diff","patch_url":"https://github.com/wieslawsoltes/SharpForge/pull/4525.patch","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/wieslawsoltes/SharpForge/issues/4525","number":4525,"state":"closed","locked":false,"title":"SF-A29-T05: add offline protocol, IL, XML and network-policy adapters","user":{"login":"wieslawsoltes","id":2297442,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjIyOTc0NDI=","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/2297442?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/wieslawsoltes","html_url":"https://github.com/wieslawsoltes","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/wieslawsoltes/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/wieslawsoltes/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/wieslawsoltes/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/wieslawsoltes/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/wieslawsoltes/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/wieslawsoltes/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/wieslawsoltes/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/wieslawsoltes/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/wieslawsoltes/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"body":"Task: SF-A29-T05.6\nRefs #1148, #1149, #1150. Complete bounded offline adapter batch; broader server/native-host and exact-image requirements remain open.\n\n## Delivered behavior\n\nAdd four fixed reviewed adapters using actual package entry points: ProtocolMessageReader framing; IL document assembly and visible-text round-trip checking; project XML/condition parsing; outbound NetworkPolicy and browser CSP generation. All use small owned literal seeds and capped input/output, propagate cancellation, and preserve unexpected errors as findings.\n\nProtocol compares whole-buffer and deterministic chunked parsing of UTF-8 LSP/DAP frames. IL reassembles its own formatted output and compares all visible directives/instructions, excluding precisely the append-only `.image` scaffold. XML condition Exists queries consult only two in-memory fixture names. Network policy checks issue no requests or sockets; native host profiles return explicit unsupported reasons.\n\n## Validation\n\n25/25 focused tests passed without skips at local `16768160`, tree `2fdd5b4866a310c04707988b7cb9b8bdcc0864be`, Node 24.19.0 / npm 11.9.0 / Linux x64.\n\n`node scripts/limited.js node --test --test-concurrency=1 --test-reporter=tap tests/conformance/fuzz/text-targets.test.js`\n\nTests cover deterministic owned seeds, configured/hard limits, cancellation, valid and invalid framing/IL/XML/policy inputs, unsupported host profiles and preservation of unexpected exceptions. Read-only review and whitespace checks completed. Required hosted core remains the published-head static/build gate; connector publication verifies tree identity while assigning commit metadata.\n\n## Exact boundaries\n\n- Protocol framing is covered; semantic LSP/DAP server request sequences are not.\n- `IL_DOCUMENT_VISIBLE_TEXT` is a narrower invariant than full serialized-document idempotence. The current CIL writer appends method bodies to `.image`; full #1149 remains unmet.\n- Native token, host Origin and host path checks are unsupported by this adapter. They are not replaced with passing NetworkPolicy checks.\n- No provider, network, external process, native runtime, filesystem extraction or full mutation campaign was executed by these focused tests.\n\nEight new files, no production changes or dependencies. No live Project claim or issue closure is asserted. Harness/campaign composition follows in a dependent batch.","created_at":"2026-10-04T11:29:01Z","updated_